<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6"><p class="font-bold">The twins meet twice, but their clocks trace different journeys.</p><svg class="w-full" viewBox="0 0 460 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="figure-title figure-desc"><title id="figure-title">The twins meet twice, but their clocks trace different journeys.</title><desc id="figure-desc">Earth remains at one position while Stella travels to a star four light years away and returns at 80 percent of light speed. Ten Earth years and six ship years pass.</desc><g fill="none" stroke-width="4"><path d="M95 231 V38" stroke="#387a91"/><path d="M95 231 L314 134 L95 38" stroke="#bd4b37"/></g><path d="M95 231 H325 M95 231 V24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><g fill="currentColor" font-size="17"><text x="10" y="40">10 years</text><text x="14" y="139">5 years</text><text x="15" y="230">0 years</text><text x="89" y="254" text-anchor="middle">Earth</text><text x="311" y="254" text-anchor="middle">Star</text><text x="130" y="70">Terence: 10 years</text><text x="180" y="108">Stella: 6 years</text><text x="336" y="137">Turn</text></g><circle cx="95" cy="231" r="5" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="95" cy="38" r="5" fill="currentColor"/></svg><figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">In the Earth frame, Stella flies at 0.8 times light speed to a star 4 light years away and back. Terence ages 10 years; Stella’s moving clock records 6. The sloping and straight lines meet at the same departure and return events. The drawn slopes are schematic.</figcaption></figure>